// Paperback's doodle art (plans/paperback/layout-1.md, *Settled in session 0*): the frames' vector
// layers, transcribed once and read by every section from here, as Lattice's `LATTICE_ART` is. Art, not
// photography, so it lives in no `photos/` file: pure SVG, no effect, no library. Every piece is the
// frame's own artwork, in the frame's own colours (the frames draw it in literals: ink #0B0B0B, pink
// #F8158F, magenta #FD48F2, yellow #FFD24A, cyan #A4F6F8, lilac #9982DE, orange #F9A12B, indigo
// #3B308F, white), so a section that stands one on another scheme re-colours it from its own call.
//
// What is here, by frame node (desktop):
//   sparkle            the four-point star at every size (header 1:2329, 1:2331; bio, gallery, map,
//                      pricing, testimonials, footer): one 16-unit path with a 0.8 stroke, which is
//                      the frames' 5% at every size (16 / 26 / 29 / 44 / 48 px read the same)
//   blobs              blush (bio 1:2398 · 560), magenta (calendar · 420), indigo (form · 360), orange
//                      (repertoire · 460): the soft shapes behind a card or a tile
//   vinyl, vinylMini   the bio's disc with its burst lines (130) and the header's sticker (39); vinylDisc and
//                      vinylBurst are the same artwork split so the disc can turn under the bio's badge states
//   arrowIndigo, arrowBlack   the bio's `that's me!` arrow (110 x 60) and the map's `home turf` arrow (90)
//   circle             the calendar's indigo scribble round the picked day (116 x 72)
//   speaker, headphones, chat, note, heart, star, trophy   the doodle icons in the white discs
//   underline          the header's pink hand-drawn underline (352 x 24)
//   confettiCalendar, confettiMap, confettiMedia   the scattered dashes behind three sections
//   rings              the map card's concentric dashed rings (657 x 447)
//   wave               the testimonials' yellow wave (1440 x 730; the frame draws two)
//   play               the media rows' triangle
// The hero's wavy field is one path (`PAPERBACK_WAVES`) the three frames crop differently, below.
//
// Arrows left and right (14 px) are lucide's, and the white and pink discs are CSS circles.
